<section class="story-section story-problem" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="story-heading"><span class="story-label">01 / THE PROBLEM</span><h2 id="problem-title">Care moves fast.<br><span>Information needs to keep up.</span></h2><p>When records, supplies, and team updates live in separate places, even a simple task can mean another follow-up.</p></div>
        <div class="story-grid">
            <article class="story-card"><span class="story-icon" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Scattered information</h3><p>Separate records make it harder to find the patient, document, or update needed for the next task.</p><span class="story-card-note">More searching. Less visibility.</span></article>
            <article class="story-card"><span class="story-icon" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Unclear supply status</h3><p>On-hand stock, procurement quantities, and deliveries need to be understood together to plan supplies.</p><span class="story-card-note">More follow-ups. More uncertainty.</span></article>
            <article class="story-card"><span class="story-icon" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Disconnected handovers</h3><p>Teams need a common place to review work, maintain documents, and coordinate across departments.</p><span class="story-card-note">More repetition between teams.</span></article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
